      "title": "Best 17 Vector Databases for 2026 [Top Picks] - lakeFS",
      "snippet": "As vector workloads mature, operational concerns – versioning, validation, and rollback – become as important as retrieval performance.\n\nVector libraries handle static similarity search, while vector databases support dynamic, production workloads.\n\nVector databases introduce operational complexity that must be managed across environments (dev, staging, production).\n\nThere is no single “best” open-source vector database, but Milvus, Weaviate, and Qdrant are the most widely adopted and production-proven choices today.\n\nNo matter which database you choose, embedding changes and index rebuilds ar",
      "content_ref": null,
