      "snippet": "- A developer's production experience with pgvector: sub-100ms queries degraded to multi-second timeouts, high memory consumption, and index build times ballooned from minutes to hours as scale increased.\n- Vectors are lists of numbers (e.g., 384–1536 dimensions) that represent semantic meaning; similar concepts have vectors close together in high-dimensional space.\n- Brute-force search is impractical at scale: comparing one million 768-dimensional vectors involves massive computation, overwhelming databases.\n- Vector indexes are specialized data structures that avoid checking every vector, reducing candidate comparisons to a few hundred or thousand for efficient similarity search.",
