    {
      "id": "ev_passage_409066679d46493b",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://encore.dev/articles/best-vector-databases",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Vector Databases in 2026: Complete Comparison Guide – Encore",
      "snippet": "* Serverless tier that auto-scales with query volume and data size\n* Namespace isolation for multi-tenant applications\n* Metadata filtering on vector results\n* Supports sparse-dense hybrid search\n* SOC 2 Type II compliance\n\n**Best for:**\n\n* Teams that want zero operational overhead for vector search\n* Multi-tenant applications at scale where per-tenant isolation matters\n* Workloads at hundreds of millions or billions of vectors\n* Organizations that need managed compliance and SLAs\n\n**Limitations:**\n\n* Proprietary, closed-source. Your data and indexes are in Pinecone's cloud.\n* Eventually consistent. Writes take time to become searchable.\n* Metadata filtering is limited compared to SQL (no joins, no subqueries).\n* Cost can scale quickly at high query volumes.\n\n**Example:**",
      "content_ref": "1107056ce809756369be8c941c0be0bcc1c2e68401ee260da9b41701a62ca569",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.294308+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 5327,
        "end_char": 6109
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_efa37f8e8e8d315f",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://encore.dev/articles/best-vector-databases",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Vector Databases in 2026: Complete Comparison Guide – Encore",
      "snippet": "```\nimport { Pinecone } from \"@pinecone-database/pinecone\";\n\nconst pc = new Pinecone({ apiKey: process.env.PINECONE_API_KEY });\nconst index = pc.index(\"documents\");\n\n// Upsert\nawait index.upsert([{\n  id: \"doc-1\",\n  values: embedding,\n  metadata: { category: \"engineering\" },\n}]);\n\n// Query\nconst results = await index.query({\n  vector: queryEmbedding,\n  topK: 10,\n  filter: { category: { $eq: \"engineering\" } },\n  includeMetadata: true,\n});\n```\n\nPinecone is the right choice when you need scale and managed infrastructure above everything else. For a detailed comparison with pgvector, see [pgvector vs Pinecone](/articles/pgvector-vs-pinecone).",
      "content_ref": "e1985589b5e6ec87bc419774b6d38f56520ba83649fb42c19f3b1405e0226149",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.294308+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 6111,
        "end_char": 6756
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_05c1e680c9e5877c",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://encore.dev/articles/best-vector-databases",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Vector Databases in 2026: Complete Comparison Guide – Encore",
      "snippet": "Qdrant is a strong choice if you need a dedicated vector database and want to stay open-source. If you're using Encore, we have a [tutorial for building semantic search with Qdrant](/blog/building-semantic-search-qdrant-encore). For a comparison with pgvector, see [pgvector vs Qdrant](/articles/pgvector-vs-qdrant).\n\n[Weaviate: Best for Built-in Vectorization](#weaviate-best-for-built-in-vectorization)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[Weaviate](https://weaviate.io/) is an open-source vector database that goes beyond storage and search. It includes built-in modules for generating embeddings, so you can insert raw text and Weaviate handles the vectorization.\n\n**Key features:**",
      "content_ref": "ee41e5286f9860156d366f682e2c34a811e2a0d771873037bd89e400e4b6cbe8",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.294308+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 8736,
        "end_char": 9474
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_44170a7933ceab9f",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://encore.dev/articles/best-vector-databases",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Vector Databases in 2026: Complete Comparison Guide – Encore",
      "snippet": "* Vectorization modules add latency and API costs (they call the same embedding APIs you'd call yourself)\n* GraphQL API adds a learning curve compared to SQL or simple REST\n* Resource-heavy for self-hosting (Java-based runtime)\n* Operational complexity increases with modules and multi-tenancy\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nimport weaviate from \"weaviate-client\";\n\nconst client = await weaviate.connectToLocal();\n\n// Insert raw text, Weaviate vectorizes it\nawait client.collections.get(\"Document\").data.insert({\n  title: \"Vector Search Guide\",\n  content: \"pgvector adds vector search to PostgreSQL...\",\n});\n\n// Semantic search\nconst results = await client.collections.get(\"Document\")\n  .query.nearText(\"how does vector search work\", { limit: 10 });\n```",
      "content_ref": "2480a7a5edbdd80c1fc633f7bb6203f5a239efc18bf6a99a780cbd783c05550a",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.294308+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 10032,
        "end_char": 10773
      }
