    {
      "id": "ev_passage_12f9f1cdfa2db87d",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://redis.io/blog/best-open-source-vector-databases-comparison",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Open Source Vector Databases 2026 & Comparison",
      "snippet": "Most vector databases solve the same core problem: store vector embeddings, find similar ones fast. The differences show up when you move from prototype to production.\n\nProduction AI apps don't run in isolation. Your retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) pipeline needs session state. Your chatbot needs rate limiting. Your recommendation engine needs real-time feature data.\n\nWith specialized vector databases, that means managing separate systems: a vector store, a cache, an operational database, and keeping them in sync. A unified platform handles vectors alongside everything else, reducing the number of systems to manage and eliminating network hops between your vector search and your cache.",
      "content_ref": "62a9ebc6e8e8e12ac959a745fdcb5038896547d2a0c55ab0160c183bcf34b3f3",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:40.790686+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 4984,
        "end_char": 5683
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_1f5bc116c316a283",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://redis.io/blog/best-open-source-vector-databases-comparison",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Open Source Vector Databases 2026 & Comparison",
      "snippet": "* **Vector search architecture:** Redis uses Hierarchical Navigable Small World ([HNSW](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.09320)) indexing for datasets exceeding 1 million documents where performance and scalability take priority, plus FLAT indexing for exact nearest neighbor search when precision requirements override performance. Supports text, image, and video vector embeddings from any model provider.\n* **Billion-scale performance:** With proper HNSW tuning, Redis achieves [95% precision](https://redis.io/blog/searching-1-billion-vectors-with-redis-8/) when searching 1 billion vectors at ~1.3s median latency. At smaller scales, [Superlinked](https://redis.io/customers/superlinked/) sustained 95th percentile latency at 30ms under heavy usage, and [Redis benchmarks](https://redis.io/blog/benchm",
      "content_ref": "d7bdc22296fef412ee7341e773c531d2427eff4992730f59e83049c89df50054",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:40.790686+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 6878,
        "end_char": 7678,
        "heading": "**Redis**",
        "heading_path": [
          "**Redis**"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_2a57b37215bb45ce",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://redis.io/blog/best-open-source-vector-databases-comparison",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "Best Open Source Vector Databases 2026 & Comparison",
      "snippet": "arking-results-for-vector-databases/) show Redis outperforming tested alternatives at recall ≥98%. Performance varies by workload, so benchmark with your actual data.\n* **Hybrid search:** The [FT.HYBRID command](https://redis.io/docs/latest/commands/ft.hybrid/) combines vector similarity with filtering on geographic, numeric, tag, or text data. [Redis 8.4](https://redis.io/blog/introducing-redis-8-4/) adds multiple ranking algorithms (Reciprocal Rank Fusion and linear combination) for score fusion.\n* **Semantic caching:** [Redis LangCache](https://redis.io/langcache/) (managed service, currently in preview) stores large language model (LLM) responses and serves cached results for semantically similar queries. You trade an embedding lookup plus similarity search for avoiding much slower LLM",
      "content_ref": "e3b4347909fe213e5354e46f3e7c5f436bfe17e70bf2f6604f3c20e742f49844",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:40.790686+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 7678,
