    {
      "id": "ev_passage_805d99e1eb4f2a33",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://liveblocks.io/blog/whats-the-best-vector-database-for-building-ai-products",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "What's the best vector database for building AI products? | Liveblocks blog",
      "snippet": "Learn more![SOC 2](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsecurity%2Fbadge-soc2.png&w=128&q=90)Learn more![HIPAA](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsecurity%2Fbadge-hipaa.png&w=128&q=90)\n\n  © 2026 Liveblocks Inc.\n\n[Blog](/blog)/[Engineering](/blog/category/engineering)\n\nWhat's the best vector database for building AI products?\n=========================================================\n\nVector databases are the backbone of retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), a key technique enabling modern AI products to deliver accurate, context-aware answers from private data. This is our comprehensive comparison of leading vector databases, including Turbopuffer, Pinecone, Qdrant, pgvector, and many more.\n\n![Picture of Jonathan Rowny](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fpeople%2Fjonathan-rowny.jpg&w=96&q=75)",
      "content_ref": "3f3d30fe94d4947b30a34363bd6c328bf46df0995e41210b60c2630a487e5872",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.326656+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
