        "end_char": 6523
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_8780a91dbd766768",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://liveblocks.io/blog/whats-the-best-vector-database-for-building-ai-products",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "What's the best vector database for building AI products? | Liveblocks blog",
      "snippet": "Jonathan Rowny on September 15th, 2025\n\n![What's the best vector database for building AI products?](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fblog%2Fthe-most-comprehensive-guide-to-choosing-the-right-vector-database-in-2025%2Fthe-most-comprehensive-guide-to-choosing-the-right-vector-database-in-2025.jpg&w=2048&q=90)\n\nSeptember 15th, 2025·23 min read\n\n* ![Picture of Jonathan Rowny](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fpeople%2Fjonathan-rowny.jpg&w=96&q=75)Jonathan Rowny\n\nShare article\n\nCopy link\n\n[AI](/blog?tags=ai)[Vector database](/blog?tags=vector-database)[RAG](/blog?tags=rag)[Machine learning](/blog?tags=machine-learning)\n\nReady to get started?\n---------------------\n\nJoin thousands of companies using Liveblocks to build multiplayer experiences for people and agents.\n\n[Get started for free](/auth/signup)",
      "content_ref": "373c2d04bfc1a744bbccd31393d98470f5aae1749e4abae2f78a10149390cf1e",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.326656+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 6525,
        "end_char": 7323
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_passage_4a99064f9a6b390f",
      "source_type": "passage",
      "provider": "direct_http",
      "url": "https://liveblocks.io/blog/whats-the-best-vector-database-for-building-ai-products",
      "document_id": null,
      "title": "What's the best vector database for building AI products? | Liveblocks blog",
      "snippet": "* **Performance & scalability**: Performance is crucial for us, as we need to\n  provide responsive AI agents for our customers. While we weren't able to\n  benchmark every solution, we'll discuss available third-party benchmarks.\n* **Features**: We focused on indexing strategies, namespace support, which give\n  us the ability to split data by type and tenant. We also quickly identified\n  that hybrid search is essential for robust RAG solutions, and because our\n  agents run close to the user on edge runtimes, an HTTP API or edge-compatible\n  SDK was a must.\n* **Limitations**: Each option varies greatly in terms of limitations,\n  particularly when it comes to indexes and namespaces.\n* **Enterprise compatibility**: As with other enterprise service providers,\n  compliance and security are key.",
      "content_ref": "fe5b63dcd40125f1e5a139f434079aa5046fc41cdfeddd95b9b296d1a54b5116",
      "published_date": null,
      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:41.326656+00:00",
      "query": null,
      "quality_score": null,
      "freshness_score": null,
      "citation_id": null,
      "metadata": {
        "start_char": 11095,
        "end_char": 11895,
        "heading": "Understanding sync engines: How Figma, Linear, and Google Docs work",
        "heading_path": [
          "Understanding sync engines: How Figma, Linear, and Google Docs work"
        ]
      }
