      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:40.933208+00:00",
      "method": "direct_http",
      "quote": "* [Pinecone](https://www.pinecone.io/): A fully-managed cloud vector DB. Known for enterprise-grade reliability and scalability. * [Turbopuffer](https://turbopuffer.com/): An S3-based serverless vector + text search engine. Cost-effective w",
      "snippet_hash": "9fa8885edbb8cd4e7da48e58de30ead4af74ec75d5cf3283983554db9b290ea7"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.zenml.io/blog/vector-databases-for-rag",
      "text": "le and high-throughput serving.\n* [Vespa](https://vespa.ai/): A full-featured search platform with vector support. Designed for billion-scale deployments.\n* [pgvector](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector) (PostgreSQL): A Postgres extension for vector columns. Brings HNSW/IVF indexing to PostgreSQL’s relational engine.\n* [Elasticsearch](https://www.elastic.co/elasticsearch): A proven distributed search engine. Combines Elasticsearch’s mature text querying and filtering with vector fields.\n* [MongoDB](https://www.mongodb.com/) (Atlas Vector Search): A document database with built-in vector search. Supports hybrid full-text and embedding search, as well as rich JSON filtering.",
      "start_char": 8315,
      "end_char": 8998,
