      "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:25:40.933208+00:00",
      "method": "direct_http",
      "quote": "### Pros and Cons The major pro is Pinecone’s simplicity and fully managed, serverless nature, which offloads infrastructure concerns for RAG developers. Its real-time indexing and powerful filtering are built for production. Pinecone also ",
      "snippet_hash": "34831ad12c23a6dee37d95e573363fda66c32a31b1282f6cc035d44bea3db525"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.zenml.io/blog/vector-databases-for-rag",
      "text": "### Pros and Cons\n\nQdrant’s open-source nature and flexible deployment are strong advantages. Many teams find their Rust core is efficient and simple to get running via Docker. An ideal choice for complex RAG applications that need to slice and dice data.\n\nHowever, it doesn’t natively do hybrid keyword search or have built-in vectorizers. By default, Qdrant is vector-only; you’d have to manage full-text search separately. Also, clustering (sharding) is relatively new in Qdrant and not as battle-tested as older DBs.\n\n6. Milvus\n---------\n\n![__wf_reserved_inherit](https://assets.zenml.io/webflow/64a817a2e7e2208272d1ce30/95826cac/68dca9c83d55484900aac8ad_milvus-homepage.webp)",
      "start_char": 23480,
      "end_char": 24160,
      "heading": "Pros and Cons",
