    {
      "url": "https://www.altexsoft.com/blog/vector-databases-compared",
      "text": "[Vector databases](https://www.altexsoft.com/blog/vector-database/) have become an invaluable part of many modern AI systems, powering everything from [AI chatbots](https://www.altexsoft.com/blog/a-technological-guide-to-building-an-ai-chatbot/) and [recommendation engines](https://www.altexsoft.com/blog/recommender-system-personalization/) to [fraud detection](https://www.altexsoft.com/whitepapers/fraud-detection-how-machine-learning-systems-help-reveal-scams-in-fintech-healthcare-and-ecommerce/) systems and intelligent document search.\n\nIn this article, we will explore some of the most popular and widely adopted solutions in the market, namely Chroma, Pinecone, Qdrant, Milvus, Weaviate, pgvector, MongoDB, and FAISS, to see how they compare so you can find the right fit for your stack.",
      "start_char": 711,
      "end_char": 1508,
