      "snippet_hash": "f48c7f3d3e8424bd9a413f147e979293debe4584360e084cf456f37f73ee90a2"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://superlinked.com/blog/choosing-a-vector-database",
      "text": "* **Brute-Force vs. Approximate:** Brute-force delivers exact results but does not scale. ANN trades a bit of accuracy for orders-of-magnitude faster queries and is standard at scale.\n* **Index Types:** Different structures (HNSW, IVF, PQ, DiskANN, etc.) have different strengths but all live on a latency/recall trade-off curve. The important question is whether the DB can hit your targets on that curve.\n* **Guaranteed Recall:** For cases demanding 100 percent recall, a common pattern is ANN for candidates plus exact reranking on a smaller subset.\n\nUsing an inference score endpoint for reranking keeps heavy compute off the vector DB and ensures consistent reranking across datasets.",
