      "url": "https://thedataquarry.com/blog/vector-db-4",
      "text": "### 3. Insertion speed vs. query speed[#](#3-insertion-speed-vs-query-speed)\n\nCertain vendors like Milvus/Zilliz, have been around for long enough that they are looking at humongous-scale streaming use cases that require vectors. Inserting, and then indexing thousands of vectors per minute may be essential in real-time scenarios like video surveillance or financial transaction tracking, and Milvus/Zilliz are capable of throwing the kitchen sink at this problem[6](#user-content-fn-5).\n\nHowever, is insertion speed that important to the majority of use cases? For most organizations, querying speed is more important. This is because insertion and indexing are typically done infrequently, but the data might be queried much more frequently, typically in real-time at scale via user interfaces.",
      "start_char": 9190,
      "end_char": 9987,
      "heading": "3. Insertion speed vs. query speed[#](#3-insertion-speed-vs-query-speed)",
      "heading_path": [
        "3. Insertion speed vs. query speed[#](#3-insertion-speed-vs-query-speed)"
      ],
      "page_title": "Vector databases (4): Analyzing the trade-offs • The Data Quarry",
